  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Eastern Air Express is an active federal contractor in FY2026 to date with total obligations of $223M across 54 awards. Eastern Air Express has an average award size of $4.1M and obligations are up 3857.5% year over year. Eastern Air Express’s FY2026 obligations are concentrated with the Department of Homeland Security, which accounts for $216M of the total, followed by the Department of Defense with $4.9M and the Department of the Interior with $3M. Eastern Air Express shows a steep rise from prior fiscal years: FY25 obligations were $5.6M, FY24 obligations were $2.2M, FY23 obligations were $2.9M, FY22 obligations were $3.3K, and FY21 obligations were $0. Current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date contract obligations rather than full-year totals. This profile points to a sudden, large increase in federal work for Eastern Air Express in FY2026 to date and a heavy reliance on one primary buyer in the current period.",
